"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resolveFilterValue"},{"type":"text","value":" once per filter before any rows\nare tested. When calling a filter function directly (outside of a table),\napply it yourself: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fn(row, columnId, fn.resolveFilterValue?.(value) ?? value)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfeatures","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFeatures"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/TableFeatures.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TableFeatures"}]},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tdata","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TData"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/RowData.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RowData"}]},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"def","children":[{"type":"text","value":"def"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/FilterFnDef.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FilterFnDef"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/CreatedFilterFn.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CreatedFilterFn"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFeatures"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"function-constructfilterfn","text":"Function: constructFilterFn()","level":1},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfeatures","text":"TFeatures","level":3},{"id":"tdata","text":"TData","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"def","text":"def","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Function: constructFilterFn()\n\n```ts\nfunction constructFilterFn<TFeatures, TData>(def): CreatedFilterFn<TFeatures, TData>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/column-filtering/filterFns.ts:40](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/column-filtering/filterFns.ts#L40)\n\nBuilds a `FilterFn` from a value-level comparator plus optional resolvers.\n\nThe `filter` comparator receives the row's data value (already passed\nthrough `resolveDataValue` when one is defined) and the filter value\n(already passed through `resolveFilterValue` by the table). Keeping\nnormalization in the resolvers means a variant of an existing filter\nfunction only has to swap the resolvers, not re-implement the comparison.\n\nThe definition is attached to the returned function, so a variant can be\ncreated by spreading a built-in filter function and overriding what differs:\n\n```ts\nconst normalize = (value: unknown) =>\n  String(value ?? '')\n    .toLowerCase()\n    .normalize('NFD')\n    .replace(/\\p{Diacritic}/gu, '')\n\nconst includesStringIgnoreDiacritics = constructFilterFn({\n  ...filterFn_includesString,\n  resolveFilterValue: normalize,\n  resolveDataValue: normalize,\n})\n```\n\nNote: the table applies `resolveFilterValue` once per filter before any rows\nare tested. When calling a filter function directly (outside of a table),\napply it yourself: `fn(row, columnId, fn.resolveFilterValue?.(value) ?? value)`.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFeatures\n\n`TFeatures` *extends* [`TableFeatures`](../interfaces/TableFeatures.md) = `any`\n\n### TData\n\n`TData` *extends* [`RowData`](../type-aliases/RowData.md) = `any`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### def\n\n[`FilterFnDef`](../interfaces/FilterFnDef.md)\\<`TFeatures`, `TData`\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n[`CreatedFilterFn`](../interfaces/CreatedFilterFn.md)\\<`TFeatures`, `TData`\\>\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: constructFilterFn\ntitle: constructFilterFn\n---\n\n# Function: constructFilterFn()\n\n```ts\nfunction constructFilterFn<TFeatures, TData>(def): CreatedFilterFn<TFeatures, TData>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [features/column-filtering/filterFns.ts:40](https://github.com/TanStack/table/blob/main/packages/table-core/src/features/column-filtering/filterFns.ts#L40)\n\nBuilds a `FilterFn` from a value-level comparator plus optional resolvers.\n\nThe `filter` comparator receives the row's data value (already passed\nthrough `resolveDataValue` when one is defined) and the filter value\n(already passed through `resolveFilterValue` by the table). Keeping\nnormalization in the resolvers means a variant of an existing filter\nfunction only has to swap the resolvers, not re-implement the comparison.\n\nThe definition is attached to the returned function, so a variant can be\ncreated by spreading a built-in filter function and overriding what differs:\n\n```ts\nconst normalize = (value: unknown) =>\n  String(value ?? '')\n    .toLowerCase()\n    .normalize('NFD')\n    .replace(/\\p{Diacritic}/gu, '')\n\nconst includesStringIgnoreDiacritics = constructFilterFn({\n  ...filterFn_includesString,\n  resolveFilterValue: normalize,\n  resolveDataValue: normalize,\n})\n```\n\nNote: the table applies `resolveFilterValue` once per filter before any rows\nare tested. When calling a filter function directly (outside of a table),\napply it yourself: `fn(row, columnId, fn.resolveFilterValue?.(value) ?? value)`.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFeatures\n\n`TFeatures` *extends* [`TableFeatures`](../interfaces/TableFeatures.md) = `any`\n\n### TData\n\n`TData` *extends* [`RowData`](../type-aliases/RowData.md) = `any`\n\n## Parameters\n\n### def\n\n[`FilterFnDef`](../interfaces/FilterFnDef.md)\\<`TFeatures`, `TData`\\>\n\n## Returns\n\n[`CreatedFilterFn`](../interfaces/CreatedFilterFn.md)\\<`TFeatures`, `TData`\\>\n"}
